            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESebastiaan and Lotte are joined by the Head of CMS, Andy Butland, to look at the highlights of the two latest Umbraco releases - versions 17.2 and 17.3.\n\n\u0026#128064; Umbraco 17.2 release notes: https://releases.umbraco.com/release/umbraco/Umbraco-CMS/17.2.0\n\u0026#128064; Umbraco 17.3 release notes: https://releases.umbraco.com/release/umbraco/Umbraco-CMS/17.3.0\n\n\u0026#127757; Matt Brailsford\u2019s blogpost on why version 17.4 is going to be \u201Ca big deal for AI\u201D: https://mattbrailsford.dev/why-umbraco-1740-is-a-big-deal-for-ai\n\n00:00 Introduction to the DevRel Deep Dive\n01:09 **Exploring Umbraco Releases 17.2 and 17.3**\n05:04 - Enhancements in User Group Management\n07:14 - Improvements in Content Management Experience\n11:40 - Central Package Management in Umbraco\n16:42 - Optimizing Content Cache Management\n18:03 - Constructive vs Destructive Work\n18:32 - Optimizing API Calls for Performance\n20:00 - Security Updates and Dependency Management\n21:51 - Implementing HMAC for Image Requests\n23:17 - Best Practices for HMAC Keys\n24:36 - Community Contributions and Open Source Practices\n25:53 - Debugging Enhancements in Razor Files\n26:38 **Upcoming Features in Umbraco 17.4**\n27:25 - Website Output Caching Improvements\n29:27 - Enhancements for AI Integration\n31:18 - Lightweight External Members for High Traffic Sites\n\n--------\n\n\u2753 Looking for help with your Umbraco projects? Visit the Forum\n https://forum.umbraco.com\n \n\u0026#128172; Want to chat with the friendly Umbraco Community? Join our Discord server\n https://discord.umbraco.com\n \n\u2709\uFE0F Got a question (or topic suggestion) for the HQ Developer Relations team?\n https://umbra.co/contact-devrel, or the \u2018contact-devrel\u2019 channel on Discord\n \n#Umbraco\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nBEgfifIP0o\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
